e they were anonymous can you  tell me how many  i want to be careful dan because as you  know  and i don't want to specify what sides  of the ball or where this frustration  lies i would say that it's  it's it's permeated throughout the  locker room we'll leave it there  but i know that with a new coaching  regime it could lead to guys not being  here next year  punished we saw it in the past guys like  allen hearns  have gone on the record and and you know  been frustrated about not getting the  ball  as it related to the receiving core and  then the ball didn't come to him so i  want to be very careful i think  i think it's also important to  distinguish there are some egos on this  team  previous coaching staffs have talked  about there would be a standard of  coaching that would be set  by jason garrett some coaches would try  to implement that  and then some of these players would in  some cases go over the head  and it was you know go to the  principal's office and they would  sort of uh back the player and that can  be frustrating  so there are i think there's a couple of  unique challenges that mike mccarthy is  dealing with one  the condensed training camp b you're  bringing in all these new coaches  you don't have the personnel you signed  up for and line item number one you're  starting quarterback  and i think it's hard to develop  relationships with these guys as men  virtually and then when you don't really  have time to sort of cuddle these guys  in your office  that you typically would at a training  camp or be able to take these guys to  dinner when you've just got to focus on  the season so  i also want to position this as saying  maybe mike doesn't have enough of his  guys still in that locker room  and that could change so i think it's  very important to be careful  about what i say here and how we could  connect the dots  jerry jones is loyal loyal to a fault  how loyal  will he be with mike mccarthy i  i think i think the leash is long with  m